module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.DiagonalConormalDerivation

/-! # Generation of affine conormal sections by the difference derivation

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 08S2, affine calculation; Tags 01KJ, 01R3 and 00RW.
(blueprint: stage3-diagonal-conormal-affine-derivation-span).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u
open CategoryTheory Opposite
namespace AlgebraicGeometry
variable {X S : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The values of a normalized difference derivation generate affine conormal sections.
Source: Stacks Project, Tag 08S2, final affine calculation; Tags 01R3 and 00RW.
(blueprint: stage3-diagonal-conormal-affine-derivation-span).
Proof: write A = Γ(X,U) and R = Γ(S,V). The open U ×_V U is affine with ring
B = A ⊗[R] A and diagonal inverse image U (Tag 01KJ). Restrict the actual kernel
sheaf to this open: since the restricted diagonal is the closed immersion induced
by multiplication B → A, this kernel is the tilde module of J = ker(B → A).
Restriction of tensor pullback identifies its sections over U with A ⊗[B] J,
and then with J/J² (Tag 01R3). The tensor-pullback unit sends a section of J to
its quotient class. The normalization hD therefore sends D(a) to the class of
1 ⊗ a - a ⊗ 1. The ideal J is generated by these differences. More precisely,
KaehlerDifferential.submodule_span_range_eq_ideal says that they span J even as
an A-module, with A acting through the first tensor factor. The surjective map
J → J/J² sends a spanning set to a spanning set, and the quotient A-action is
the conormal A-action. Transporting the span equality back to the actual sections
gives the stated equality. No injectivity of any differential comparison map is
needed. If U is empty both modules are zero; if f is an open immersion the local
multiplication ideal is zero. Nonseparated f causes no problem because this uses
only the closed diagonal inside U ×_V U. -/
theorem diagonalConormal_affine_derivation_span (f : X ⟶ S)
    (U : X.affineOpens) (V : S.affineOpens) (hUV : U.1 ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V.1)
    (D : (diagonalConormal f).val.Derivation' f.pullbackPresheafToPresheaf)
    (hD : IsDiagonalConormalDerivation f D) :
    Submodule.span Γ(X, U.1) (Set.range (fun a : Γ(X, U.1) ↦
      D.d (X := op U.1) a)) = ⊤ := by sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
